  "definition": "A geodetic datum relates a coordinate system to the Earth. It supplies the origin, orientation and scale needed to turn mathematical coordinates into positions. An ellipsoid supplies a model of the Earth's size and shape, but is only one part of this relationship: different datums or frames can use the same ellipsoid and still assign different coordinates to a point.[^1][^2]",
